Package: sharedstat
Title: Diagnose and Correct Statistics Built from a Shared Component
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Rui", "Chen", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "Rui.Chen@campus.lmu.de")
Author: Rui Chen [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Rui Chen <Rui.Chen@campus.lmu.de>
Description: Comparative designs often form a statistic from a difference, a ratio or a residual
    of two quantities that share a measured component: a divergence measured against a shared
    reference arm, a 'trans' term obtained by subtracting a 'cis' term, a count of significant
    genes read as an ordering of effect sizes, or an interaction contrast on compositional counts.
    In each case the shared measurement error enters the statistic twice with opposite signs, so
    the estimate is biased by a factor depending on the reliability of the shared component, and
    the bias does not shrink as features are added. This package quantifies that bias for a given
    design, applies an instrumental-variable correction where an instrument is available, and
    provides a known-truth simulator in which compositionality emerges from closed-sum sampling
    rather than being imposed.
